{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families","id":1376631,"title":"Does being an Awakened mage run in families?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-25T17:35:15-07:00","id":1376631,"title":"Does being an Awakened mage run in families?","content":"I\u2019m asking because I heard that the Merovingian bloodline from the movie The Da Vinci Code are actually part of the Celestial Chorus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T17:45:44-07:00","id":1376633,"title":"","content":"Its not really a blood thing, so much as it is a possible thing from being human. Basically if you're not a superntural then you're a sleeper and not really any big probability thing between blood towards not being a sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T18:03:15-07:00","id":1376635,"title":"","content":"Awakenings explicitly do not run in families, although there is nothing preventing you from saying that it does pass down through this particular bloodline, then make that into its own Mystery as to why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T19:39:29-07:00","id":1376646,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> <br /> But what about the Merovingians? Are they a real canon thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T19:43:15-07:00","id":1376648,"title":"","content":"Celestial Chorus Revised Tradition Book, pp. 83\u201384.<br /> <br /> It's mentioned in a section about Legends of the Chorus, and is prefaced with a warning that \u201cthe following legends are well known to most Choristers. No Singer has yet discovered the truth behind any of them. Perhaps the future will reveal their meaning, or perhaps they are myth, shaped by belief as much as anything else.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-25-2020, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T19:53:04-07:00","id":1376651,"title":"","content":"My own view is that the hard answer is \u201cno.\u201d<br /> <br /> However, it\u2019s not really all that outlandish that mages would find themselves attracted to other mages, and in turn, their offspring would be exposed to quite a bit that would predispose them to awakening. In my chronicles, it\u2019s not unheard of for there to be multigenerational patterns of mages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:44:33-07:00","id":1376661,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> thanks \ud83d\ude0a. So it might just be a myth in-canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:46:25-07:00","id":1376662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1376633#post1376633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not really a blood thing, so much as it is a possible thing from being human. Basically if you're not a superntural then you're a sleeper and not really any big probability thing between blood towards not being a sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the books have explicitly said in multiple Areas that Awakening is the Legacy of certain families and bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:48:31-07:00","id":1376663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1376635#post1376635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awakenings explicitly do not run in families, although there is nothing preventing you from saying that it does pass down through this particular bloodline, then make that into its own Mystery as to why.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books mentioned explicitly they do run in certain families, like with Verbena family having a proclivity to producing a witch daughter once every generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T22:57:50-07:00","id":1376668,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thank you \ud83d\ude0a. That\u2019s what I was wondering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T23:05:47-07:00","id":1376672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1376661#post1376661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> thanks \ud83d\ude0a. So it might just be a myth in-canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just \u201cmight be\u201d. There's a box on the cited page that basically says that unless you're running a Chorister-centric Chronicle, the Merovingian myth is almost certainly false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T06:49:34-07:00","id":1376705,"title":"","content":"Most of the mage families are actually sorcerers.<br /> <br /> You could argue, perhaps, that in magical families avatars tend reincarnate withing the family/ Mages have stronger avatars than the general population so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T08:17:23-07:00","id":1376717,"title":"","content":"The Verbena certainly do believe that magick runs (or at least that it *can* run) in the blood...but there's no proof of that, and most mage groups don't think this is the case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T15:24:25-07:00","id":1376741,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> cool. I never really got that movie anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T15:36:47-07:00","id":1376744,"title":"","content":"What movie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T18:45:58-07:00","id":1376759,"title":"","content":"I'd assume The Da Vinci Code as referenced in the OP.<br /> <br /> Though my answer to the question would be: this is Mage, things that aren't &quot;true&quot; in the setting happen all the time if mages work at it hard enough. Does magic run in the blood? No... until mages that believe in magical bloodlines do so hard enough it at least happens for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T23:19:37-07:00","id":1376784,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Though some things are easier to mess with than others; and \u201cwhere powerful Avatars end up and whether or not they Awaken\u201d strikes me as one of the harder things to change \u2014 especially if you want it to be a lasting change that carries over from generation to generation. That is, you're not just messing with the destiny of Avatars (which by definition are the things in the setting that are <i>most</i> likely to be able to say \u201cno\u201d to magical attempts to influence or control them); you're trying to establish an influence that will persist into the future \u2014 something that has what MRev called Historical Inertia. Otherwise, your family's magical birthright will die out just as soon as people stop believing in it; and considering how much belief is likely to be necessary to make such a thing possible, it wouldn't take much to cause it to die out. <br /> <br /> That said, MRev also had something in it about psychopomp spirits that exist to guide Avatars to their proper hosts; and Dark Ages suggested the possibility that the reason why their era of mages never heard voices in their heads was that the psychopomps were doing an exceptional job matching the two. I don't really buy the latter; but if the former is true, then I could see the <i>psychopomps</i> being influenced to send an inordinate number of powerful Avatars to a particular family. I still don't think it would help with the Awakenings of those Avatars (the psychopomps, even if they exist, have nothing to do with that); but it would increase the number of potent Avatars in the family. <br /> <br /> I strongly agree with the idea posted earlier in this thread that magic that runs in the family is going to be more like Sorcery than Awakened Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T05:14:18-07:00","id":1376800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1376759#post1376759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though my answer to the question would be: this is Mage, things that aren't &quot;true&quot; in the setting happen all the time if mages work at it hard enough. Does magic run in the blood? No... until mages that believe in magical bloodlines do so hard enough it at least happens for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> w/o entering in Avatar manipulation or psychopomps (that could make this stuff into a technique), I would chalk this as similar as how Hermetic &quot;study hermeticism&quot; method seems to work to Awaken people, but the ratio of failure it's still way too high to prove to others that it actually *does* work.<br /> <br /> If Hermetics get this &quot;bonus&quot;, why not others? Verbena could have discovered that magical families seem to have a higher &quot;Awakening ratio&quot;, but it would still be far from exact science, and not a big enough thing as to prove anything to another faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T12:47:49-07:00","id":1376839,"title":"","content":"It's also all &quot;fluff&quot; anyway. If I want a character with a magical bloodline that links into Backgrounds like Destiny, Legend, Familiar, and so on, or various Merits/Flaws (esp. supernatural ones), then they get to at least believe in their magical bloodlines, and have mechanics that at least back of those beliefs (like all mages do for how they view things). It's just adding details and quirks to my character; which is cool. Just like Mage-Hogwarts raised Hermetics can be cool to do. Or an Akashayana raised in a monastery and learned enlightened teachings etc. etc.<br /> <br /> There's no need to worry about the grander scheme of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T14:20:10-07:00","id":1376855,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> The Da Vinci Code<br /> <br /> \u201cSaladin\u2019s army routs the Crusaders at the battle of Hattin in 1187, killing the last king of Jerusalem and basically ending the Merovingian bloodline.\u201d<br /> <br /> Just a thought I had. I like it better than the official explanation in the Celestial Chorus book that all the Merovingian mages just disappeared one day (I went back and reread the book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T14:55:26-07:00","id":1376859,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. The whole idea of the Merovingian bloodline is really elitist. The idea that you can be Awakened based on who your family is rather than on your own merits.<br /> <br /> \u201cMa always said the Keanes were kings of Ireland back in the day, but I\u2019d rather be part of the untitled aristocracy today than the titled aristocracy twenty generations back.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jay McInerney, Last of the Savages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T15:37:44-07:00","id":1376865,"title":"","content":"Well, you don't actually Awaken based on your own merits either. Lots of characters that have done nothing of note before Awakening become mages.<br /> <br /> Awakening is always either going to be random, or elitist on some level. There isn't some universal arbiter of merit passing out power in the setting, so any construction of merit based Awakenings is based on biased values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T16:48:13-07:00","id":1376868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1376855#post1376855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cSaladin\u2019s army routs the Crusaders at the battle of Hattin in 1187, killing the last king of Jerusalem and basically ending the Merovingian bloodline.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The last King of Jerusalem was Guy of Lusignan, and while he was captured at the battle of Hattin, Saladin spared his life, kept him prisoner for a year and then let him go. He eventually ended up as the King of Cyprus for a few years before his death in 1194, with his younger brother succeeding him. Guy is from the House of Lusignan, which originated in the Poitou area of western France in the 10th century. While they don't have any known connection to the Merovingian Dynasty (not that you couldn't invent a fictional one if you wanted to), they actually have a couple of interesting stories of their own. There's a series of medieval folk tales and stories about Melusine, a female spirit/faerie/something connected to fresh water and sacred springs. These stories mostly came from the British Isles, Northern France and the Low Countries, IIRC, with one of them that she personally built the Chateau de Lusignan with magic as gift for her husband &quot;Raymond&quot;, who may or may not be Hugh I/Hugh Venator (&quot;huntsman&quot; or &quot;hunter&quot;), the founder of the House of Lusignan. This is one of a number of variations of the Melusine story, in which she marries a minor nobleman or night with the promise that he never witness her bathing. Naturally, he eventually sees her bathing in her true form, and she gets mad, turns into a dragon, and flies away. However, this story usually involves them having a number of children, and her continuing to watch over and protect them and their decedents. It's one of those things that makes a pretty cool family background for a Hermetic, Verbena or other mage. <br /> <br /> Guy became King of Jerusalem by marrying Sibylla, Queen of Jerusalem (who was crowned after the deaths of both her brother and her young son from a previous - and very brief - marriage). They had actually already been married, but when her son died, a number of regional power players demanded she have her marriage to Guy annulled and pick a new husband to ensure strong allies for the kingdom. She agreed, on the condition that she got to pick her new husband. And as soon as she was crowned Queen, she announced she was remarrying Guy and he was going to be the King. She, along with the two daughters she had with Guy, died of disease shortly after he was released by Saladin. She was part of the House of Chateaundun from Anjou, which I don't think is considered to have any ties to the Merovingians either, as far as I know. But she is distantly related to Eleanor of Aquitaine and Richard the Lionhearted. <br /> <br /> As near as I am aware (and I don't pretend to be an expert), the idea of the Merovingians being somehow blood decedents of Christ didn't come up until several centuries after they'd been supplanted by Charles Martel (the Hammer) and the Carolingian Dynasty. But like the Lusignan, they have some interesting stuff to play around with. The dynasty was founded by Clovis I, but his grandfather Merovech is the legendary founder of the line, and in some stories is the son of some sort of five-horned sea monster referred to as &quot;the beast of Neptune&quot;. This &quot;descended from a fish&quot; concept is what the authors of The Holy Blood &amp; The Holy Grail used as the basis for the &quot;descended from Jesus&quot; idea (which they've largely since admitted was a hoax). I personally think Robert Anton Wilson's The Historical Illuminatus Chronicles has a much more interesting take in which the Merovingian line are human-alien hybrids that resemble HP Lovecraft's Deep Ones and their Innsmouth hybrids. <br /> <br /> In my own games, I have a faction within the Celestial Chorus who devote themselves to cultivating and protecting various &quot;sacred bloodlines&quot;. While some of them are fixated on the whole Priory of Sion thing, others involve the descendants of the Incan royal family, the Japanese royal family, and various Indian and African linages. When and if members of said lines Awaken, they trying to scoop them up and initiate them as quickly as possible. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T17:04:19-07:00","id":1376872,"title":"","content":"As far as Awakening running in a family line, my answer is &quot;maybe&quot;. I don't thing Mage ever said anything official about it one way or another (at least not pre-M20). My own take is that Avatars are at least semi-sentient, and will at times develop a preference for certain recurring traits, including genetics (as well as possibly reincarnated souls, certain beliefs or personality types, etc.). And families where this happens will frequently end up including a lot of Acolytes and even Sorcerers as they become involved with the Tradition or Craft (or even Convention). This includes the Akashic Brotherhood's 48 Clans of the Vajrapani, various Verbena families (such as the Crombys) including those that try to trace their lineage back to the Wyck, Etherite attempts to create Doc Savage and Tom Strong lines of supermen, &quot;cursed&quot; Hollow One families, and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T05:58:31-07:00","id":1376951,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> thank you!!! This is really helpful. I thought Baldwin IV was the last king of Jerusalem, but I think I might have gotten that from the movie Kingdom of Heaven.<br /> <br /> I love learning about historical stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T06:43:26-07:00","id":1376956,"title":"","content":"I want to say that Baldwin IV was Sibylla's brother (who died a few years before this), and Baldwin V was her son who died very young, turning her from regent to queen, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T09:17:05-07:00","id":1376970,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s true. I just forgot about Guy of Lusignan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T12:50:08-07:00","id":1376986,"title":"","content":"The thing about bloodlines is that they're actually family trees: they tend to branch out all over the place, and cutting off a single branch (e.g., killing the King of Jerusalem) doesn't eliminate any of the other branches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T18:52:29-07:00","id":1377038,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> true...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T21:35:59-07:00","id":1377065,"title":"","content":"It could be a consensual reality thing that becomes a sort of 'static' consequence because its prevalent enough in popular belief. Especially if you include all the different flavors of numina (True Faith and the Celestia Chorus approach to dynamic magic have a number of options for how they correlate, for example. Nevermind things like theurgy) There's various ways numina could be 'tied' to bloodlines (or belief could tie them to bloodlines) and out of that you might have a True mage arise (think 'struggling awake' merit in Sorcerer Revised). As Aleph notes the other traditions could have their own approaches to a hermetic 'bonus' and it may stem from some sort of collective exposure to things that increase the odds of triggering an awakening. And that's before you add in Aleph mentioning psychopomps and avatar manipulation as variables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T21:55:00-07:00","id":1377070,"title":"","content":"Somewhere I have written out a theoretical outline for a better version of the Acolyte sourcebook Ascension's Right Hand, which in addition to a bunch of acolyte centered organizations, included an entire chapter on mystical family bloodlines like the Euthanatos Pallottino, the Fenian sorcerers, the Akashic martial arts clans, descendants of the Nephilim, and what was pretty much the Addams Family. I'd kind of like to expand it in to something that covers the whole WoD, with revenants, kinfolk, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T21:58:13-07:00","id":1377072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1377070#post1377070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhere I have written out a theoretical outline for a better version of the Acolyte sourcebook Ascension's Right Hand, which in addition to a bunch of acolyte centered organizations, included an entire chapter on mystical family bloodlines like the Euthanatos Pallottino, the Fenian sorcerers, the Akashic martial arts clans, descendants of the Nephilim, and what was pretty much the Addams Family. I'd kind of like to expand it in to something that covers the whole WoD, with revenants, kinfolk, and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would snatch a product like that up in a minute. Especially if it branched into weird families of multiple gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:29:17-07:00","id":1377090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1377070#post1377070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhere I have written out a theoretical outline for a better version of the Acolyte sourcebook Ascension's Right Hand, which in addition to a bunch of acolyte centered organizations, included an entire chapter on mystical family bloodlines like the Euthanatos Pallottino, the Fenian sorcerers, the Akashic martial arts clans, descendants of the Nephilim, and what was pretty much the Addams Family. I'd kind of like to expand it in to something that covers the whole WoD, with revenants, kinfolk, and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered attempting to write it up for Storyteller's Vault? Like Eldagusto, I'd buy it in a minute. (Mind you, you'd probably want to write it up as a companion for Sorcerer Revised or Hunters Hunted 2, in the sense of referring the reader there for the mechanics of Path Magic and Psychic Phenomena.) <br /> <br /> For the record, I have no problem with magically empowered bloodlines in Mage; but I'd keep them strictly separate from the Awakened themselves: there might be rumors of members of these magical families being more likely to Awaken; but they'd strictly be rumors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:42:33-07:00","id":1377095,"title":"","content":"It's maybe number 4 or 5 on a list of projects I'd like to do. (#1 is a book of Jati for the Ravnos.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T22:54:24-07:00","id":1377099,"title":"","content":"I sympathize; I've got a list of four projects I'd like to get published on STV, if I can just get the time to get them put together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T01:40:57-07:00","id":1377135,"title":"","content":"So it seems like the general consensus is \u201cNo.\u201d Thanks guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T01:46:56-07:00","id":1377137,"title":"","content":"Not as whole families of <i>Awakened</i>, no. But I strongly support No One of Consequence's suggestion of whole families of <i>Sorcerers, Psychics, and other supernaturally empowered mortals</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T03:27:50-07:00","id":1377143,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T17:19:10-07:00","id":1377242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1376631-does-being-an-awakened-mage-run-in-families?p=1377135#post1377135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it seems like the general consensus is \u201cNo.\u201d Thanks guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more of a &quot;kinda&quot;. You do have cases like the Pallottino from Guide to the Traditions and Euthanatos Revised, as well as the Akashic martial arts clans, and Verbena Wyck bloodlines. But exactly how much of it is a blood-affinity for Awakening vs certain Avatars seeming to have an affinity for certain bloodlines is subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T20:03:51-07:00","id":1377268,"title":"","content":"To clarify: the Pallottino, Akashic martial arts clans, Verbena Wyck bloodlines, Hermetic acolytes, etc. are all primarily custos: they have access to supernatural powers but not to Sphere Magick, for the most part. A handful in each of these groups Awaken, and some claim that the percentages of Awakenings are higher than in the general population; but if so, that increase in frequency isn't enough; even with these things, the overwhelming majority of these custos families never Awaken. For the sake of argument, let's say that the odds of Awakening in the general populace is one in a million: in one of these custos families, those odds may improve to, say, one in a thousand. That's a thousand-fold improvement over the general public, which is incredible. But it's still a low enough probability that you'd probably need a gathering of every living member of a given custos family before you're likely to encounter even one Awakened family member. <br /> <br /> So you're extremely unlikely to have \u201cmom and dad are Awakened; so am I, and so are all of my siblings\u201d <i>anywhere</i> in the Mage setting; and these custos families are no different in that regard. How they <i>are</i> different is that \u201cmom and dad are sorcerers; so am I, and so are all of my siblings\u201d <i>is</i> possible in a custos family. Still unlikely; but not virtually impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T20:44:33-07:00","id":1377271,"title":"","content":"As others have said, Awakenings are generally disconnected from lineage. The important part about getting Sphere magick is to have a personal, mind-expanding revelation about the nature of Reality and what is possible. Anyone can have that.<br /> <br /> That said, many family lines pass on Linear magical power, as Sorcerers (or Psychics, etc). If a member of such bloodline became a Mage, the family is liable to see them as &quot;particularly strong in the Gift&quot;. Whereas the children of Awakened family members may have high expectations placed on them, and/or being seen as a disappointment for being a &quot;step down&quot; in comparison to their Awakened forebears. Aside from being a good source of drama, though, that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> The books leave open the possibility of certain families having regular instances of True Magick. They tend to frame such a thing as unusual, a fact likely to attract attention. In short, less an assumed normal than a source of stories unto itself because of its rarity.<br /> <br /> Also as others have said, people can certainly BELIEVE that magical power is strong in a certain lineage. They may even believe the magic is literally in their blood. In these cases, the &quot;family magical practice&quot; may use Blood and Blood Sacrifice as an Instrument in their spellcasting. No other blood may do, only that of the family. (A fact which may lead to its practitioners - Awakened or otherwise - having the Blood Magic flaw; this is not required, though).<br /> <br /> (As an aside, while a family who uses their own blood for their own magic is to be expected, you could have a situation where <i>another</i> family uses that blood for <i>their</i> magic. They may be the servants of the magical bloodline...or it could be the other way around. I can certainly see wicked Sorcerers who keep another family in bondage, because they don't think magic is possible - or at least as effective - without their &quot;magic blood&quot;.)<br /> <br /> I think the proper way to think of it is this: Magic is real, but only because we MAKE it real. You can substitute &quot;Magic&quot; for any specific aspect of mysticism, fantasy, or science fiction, and it'll apply. In Mage: The Ascension, everything is potentially true, even if only in specific instances or under certain conditions. This is why the true nature of Avatars is left deliberately vague or ambiguous. For some they are merely an aspect of the subconscious, for others a guardian angel, for others a Totem or even ancestral spirit. None of these theories are necessarily wrong, so long as they are believed in. A magical lineage is much the same. Awakening is not inherited...<i>except when it is</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T21:13:01-07:00","id":1377273,"title":"","content":"This is great \ud83d\ude0a. This really clarifies things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T16:25:04-07:00","id":1377406,"title":"","content":"In the revised Sorcerer book they mentioned an Irish family that had large numbers of Mages, Changelings, Kinane, Garou, and Garou Kinfolk who can use Gnosis, in it. So some families tend to produce multiple Mages or other Supernaturals. But far more Mages come from families without a tendency toward producing Mages than come from such families. And no Trad or other group has a monopoly on that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> If you look in at least one of the corebooks you'll see options like &quot;Honored Lineage&quot; for family connections that rise your status and open doors. They also have &quot;Accursed Lineage&quot; for family connections that get you lowered status and doors slammed in your face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-30-2020, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T22:33:25-07:00","id":1377658,"title":"","content":"My way of seeing it is the rare family that regularly produce Mages (who are one in a million) is a way to explain how some rare branches of a tradition or crafts survived with a small population. While most mage traditions and crafts have to recruit from a much wider pool of human beings because awakening is rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T02:02:04-07:00","id":1377689,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> that totally makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}